course: dictionary
lesson: 272
title: Amblyopia, or lazy eye
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Your two eyes usually work as a team, and your brain joins the two pictures into one clear view. Sometimes one eye does not see as sharply as the other. «A lazy eye, or amblyopia, means one eye has not developed sharp vision.» The word sounds like a problem with effort, but the name is only a nickname.
explain: Why does this happen? The brain uses the stronger eye more, so the weaker eye gets less practice at seeing clearly. Think of a football team where one player never gets the ball. Amblyopia is the proper word for this eye problem, and «lazy eye» is the everyday name for it.
explain: Doctors can help with an eye patch. «Covering the good eye with a patch makes the brain use the weaker one.» Wearing a patch may feel annoying, but it gives the weak eye the practice it needs. If you wear one, ask your doctor or teacher to explain how it works.
fact: Amblyopia is an eye problem where one eye does not see clearly.
fact: «Lazy eye» is the everyday name for amblyopia.
fact: Amblyopia happens because the brain uses one eye more than the other.
fact: Treatment works best in early childhood, so eye checks when you are young are important.
fact: If it is left untreated, the weak eye's sight can stay poor for life.
exercise: What is amblyopia? | *An eye problem where one eye does not see clearly | A type of eye drop | A kind of glasses frame | A problem with your ears that stops you hearing
exercise: Which everyday name means the same as amblyopia? | *Lazy eye | Red eye | Blue eye | Tired eye
exercise: Why might a doctor cover the good eye with a patch? | To make the eye bigger | *To make the brain use the weaker eye more | To make the good eye stop seeing completely | To keep the good eye dry
test: According to the lesson, when does treatment work best? | Only after you finish school | Never, because it cannot help | *In early childhood | Only in old age
test: What can happen if a lazy eye is left untreated? | *The weak eye's sight can stay poor for life | The good eye stops working | Nothing at all changes | Glasses are never needed
exam: Ella's friend says amblyopia means her brain cannot hear well. What is the correct meaning? | *One eye does not see clearly because the brain uses the other eye more | Her brain cannot hear well | She cannot close her eyes | Her eyes can only see colours
